  "sections": [
    {
      "body": "This subspace is framed around the transition from theoretical quantum advantage to experimentally constrained quantum technologies. The NISQ evidence treats devices with roughly 50 to a few hundred noisy qubits as a classically hard regime, but not as general-purpose fault-tolerant machines. The Sycamore evidence supplies a concrete random-circuit sampling milestone, while the network, variational, and machine-learning sources broaden the frame from isolated processors to interfaces, short-coherence algorithms, and conditional data-analysis speedups.",
