    {
      "body": "The evidence base mixes review synthesis with laboratory demonstrations. Preskill supplies a conceptual and error-budget framing for NISQ limits. The Sycamore source uses a programmable 53-qubit superconducting processor, XEB, elided-circuit fidelity estimates, and classical simulation comparisons. Kimble surveys cavity-QED, EIT, and DLCZ-style interfaces for quantum networking. The photonic VQE work demonstrates a two-qubit integrated processor and expectation-estimation loop for He-H+ energies, while the QML review catalogs algorithmic primitives and the assumptions needed for end-to-end advantage.",
