    },
    {
      "body": "The open questions are practical and comparative. The corpus does not resolve whether NISQ hybrid algorithms can beat mature classical heuristics, how quickly lower error rates can reduce fault-tolerance overhead, or which benchmarks establish useful quantum advantage beyond random sampling. It also leaves open how scalable networks should verify entanglement without exponential tomography, and whether quantum machine-learning pipelines can supply input, preserve speedups through circuit implementation, and extract useful classical outputs without erasing the promised advantage.",
